Package: rumdl
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: fast Markdown linter and formatter written in Rust
 rumdl checks Markdown files against the markdownlint rule set (MD001 onwards)
 and reports violations with precise line and column positions, but does the
 work in a fraction of the time the Node.js implementations take. Most rules
 can also fix themselves, so "rumdl check --fix" and "rumdl fmt" repair a tree
 in place instead of only complaining about it.
 .
 Configuration lives in rumdl.toml, .rumdl.toml or a [tool.rumdl] section of
 pyproject.toml, and an existing markdownlint configuration can be converted
 with "rumdl import". Individual rules are documented in the binary itself via
 "rumdl rule" and "rumdl explain".
 .
 A Language Server is built in ("rumdl server"), which gives diagnostics and
 fix-on-save in any LSP-capable editor without a separate package.
